---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="JSON Formatter & Validator — Free Online JSON Tool"
    description="Format, validate, and beautify JSON online. Free JSON formatter with syntax error detection. No signup required."
>
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-3">
            JSON Formatter & Validator
        </h1>
        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
            Paste your JSON below to format, validate, and beautify it. Errors
            will be highlighted.
        </p>

        <div class="flex gap-3 mb-4 flex-wrap">
            <button
                id="format-btn"
                class="px-5 py-2 bg-blue-600 text-white rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-700 text-sm font-medium"
            >
                Format
            </button>
            <button
                id="minify-btn"
                class="px-5 py-2 bg-gray-200 text-gray-800 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-300 text-sm font-medium"
            >
                Minify
            </button>
            <button
                id="copy-btn"
                class="px-5 py-2 bg-gray-200 text-gray-800 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-300 text-sm font-medium"
            >
                Copy
            </button>
            <button
                id="clear-btn"
                class="px-5 py-2 bg-gray-200 text-gray-800 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-300 text-sm font-medium"
            >
                Clear
            </button>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            <div>
                <label class="block text-sm font-medium mb-2">Input JSON</label>
                <textarea
                    id="json-input"
                    class="w-full h-96 p-4 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg font-mono text-sm focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500 resize-y"
                    placeholder='{"name": "John", "age": 30}'></textarea>
            </div>
            <div>
                <label class="block text-sm font-medium mb-2">Output</label>
                <textarea
                    id="json-output"
                    readonly
                    class="w-full h-96 p-4 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg font-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 focus:outline-none resize-y"
                    placeholder="Formatted output will appear here..."
                ></textarea>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div id="status" class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium"></div>
    </div>
    <!-- SEO Content (800+ words) -->
    <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-16">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">About This JSON Formatter</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            This free online JSON formatter and validator helps developers
            format, beautify, and validate JSON data instantly. It detects
            syntax errors and shows clear messages so you can fix your JSON
            quickly. Everything runs in your browser — your data never leaves
            your device.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            JSON is the standard data format for APIs, config files, and web
            apps. But raw JSON from a server or log file is often minified — a
            single long line that's impossible to read. This tool turns that
            mess into clean, indented, human-readable JSON in one click. It also
            catches syntax errors with exact positions, so you know exactly
            where to look.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">How to Use</h3>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
            <li>Paste your JSON into the input box (or type it directly).</li>
            <li>Click "Format" to beautify it with 2-space indentation.</li>
            <li>
                Click "Minify" to remove all whitespace and produce a
                single-line JSON string.
            </li>
            <li>
                Use "Copy" to copy the result to your clipboard, or "Clear" to
                start over.
            </li>
        </ol>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">Why Use This Tool?</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
            <li>
                <strong>Instant formatting:</strong> Paste and click — no waiting,
                no loading.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Error detection:</strong> Invalid JSON shows the exact error
                message so you can fix it fast.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Privacy first:</strong> Everything runs in your browser. No
                data is sent to any server.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Free with no limits:</strong> Format as many JSON files as
                you want, as often as you want.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Works on any device:</strong> Desktop, laptop, tablet, or
                phone — no app needed.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">
            Common JSON Errors This Tool Catches
        </h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
            <li>
                <strong>Trailing commas:</strong> A comma after the last item breaks
                JSON. This tool catches it instantly.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Single quotes:</strong> JSON only accepts double quotes. Single
                quotes cause parsing errors.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Unquoted keys:</strong> Object keys must be in double quotes
                in JSON.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Missing brackets:</strong> Unclosed objects or arrays produce
                clear error messages.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Invalid values:</strong>
                <code>undefined</code>, comments, and other non-JSON values are
                detected.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">Real Use Cases</h3>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">1. Debugging API Responses</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            When an API returns minified JSON, it's nearly impossible to read.
            Paste it here, click "Format," and you'll see the full structure —
            nested objects, arrays, and values — all neatly indented.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">2. Validating Config Files</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            A missing comma in a <code>package.json</code> or <code
                >tsconfig.json</code
            > file can break your entire build. Paste the file here to verify it's
            valid before committing.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">
            3. Preparing Data for an API Request
        </h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Many APIs require minified JSON in POST requests. Use the "Minify"
            button to compress your JSON into a single line — ready to paste
            into a request body.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">4. Learning JSON Structure</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            If you're new to JSON, formatting real examples is one of the
            fastest ways to learn. You can see exactly how nested objects and
            arrays are structured.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">5. Cleaning Up Log Files</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            JSON logs are often stored as one line per event. Formatting makes
            them readable and easier to analyze.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">A Worked Example</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Here's what happens when you paste this minified JSON:
        </p>
        <pre
            class="bg-gray-100 p-4 rounded-lg text-sm overflow-x-auto mb-4"><code>{`{"name":"Ali","age":25,"skills":["HTML","CSS","JS"]}`}</code></pre>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            After clicking "Format," the output becomes:
        </p>
        <pre
            class="bg-gray-100 p-4 rounded-lg text-sm overflow-x-auto mb-4"><code>{`{
  "name": "Ali",
  "age": 25,
  "skills": [
    "HTML",
    "CSS",
    "JS"
  ]
}`}</code></pre>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            That's the difference between an unreadable line and a clearly
            structured document. The formatted version is what you'd want to
            work with in VS Code, an API tool, or a browser console.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">Understanding JSON</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            JSON (JavaScript Object Notation) is a lightweight text format for
            storing and exchanging data. It uses two structures:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
            <li>
                <strong>Objects:</strong> Key-value pairs wrapped in curly braces,
                e.g., <code>&#123;"name": "Ali"&#125;</code>.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Arrays:</strong> Ordered lists wrapped in square brackets,
                e.g., <code>["HTML", "CSS", "JS"]</code>.
            </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mt-4 mb-4">
            JSON supports only six data types: strings, numbers, booleans, null,
            objects, and arrays. It does <strong>not</strong> support dates, functions,
            or comments. If you need dates, store them as ISO strings (<code
                >"2026-10-20"</code
            >).
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">
            Frequently Asked Questions
        </h3>
        <div class="space-y-4 mt-3">
            <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    Is my JSON data safe?
                </h4>
                <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                    Yes. All formatting and validation happens in your browser.
                    No data is sent to any server. Your JSON never leaves your
                    device.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">What is JSON?</h4>
                <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                    JSON (JavaScript Object Notation) is a lightweight data
                    format used to exchange data between servers and web
                    applications. It is easy for humans to read and machines to
                    parse.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    Does this tool support large JSON files?
                </h4>
                <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                    Yes, it can handle large JSON files. Performance depends on
                    your browser and device memory. If you're formatting files
                    over 50 MB, consider using a desktop tool like VS Code or jq
                    instead.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    Can I use comments in JSON?
                </h4>
                <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                    No. Standard JSON has no comment syntax. If you need
                    comments, use JSONC (used by VS Code) or YAML — but note
                    that most APIs won't accept either.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    What's the difference between Format and Minify?
                </h4>
                <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                    Format adds indentation and line breaks to make JSON
                    human-readable. Minify removes all whitespace to make the
                    JSON as compact as possible — useful for sending over the
                    network.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Is this tool free?</h4>
                <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                    Yes, completely free with no signup, no limits, and no
                    watermarks.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Related Tools & Guides -->
    <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-16">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Related Tools</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-10">
            <a
                href="/tools/word-counter/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Word Counter</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Count words, characters, and reading time.
                </p>
            </a>
            <a
                href="/tools/password-generator/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Password Generator</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Create strong, random passwords.
                </p>
            </a>
            <a
                href="/tools/unit-converter/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Unit Converter</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Convert length, weight, and temperature.
                </p>
            </a>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Related Guides</h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
            <a
                href="/blog/json-explained/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-medium">JSON Explained: A Beginner's Guide</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Learn JSON from scratch.</p>
            </a>
            <a
                href="/blog/common-json-errors/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-medium">
                    10 Common JSON Errors and How to Fix Them
                </h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Fix JSON syntax errors fast.
                </p>
            </a>
            <a
                href="/blog/json-vs-xml/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-medium">JSON vs XML: What's the Difference?</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Choose the right data format.
                </p>
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <script>
        const input = document.getElementById(
            "json-input",
        ) as HTMLTextAreaElement;
        const output = document.getElementById(
            "json-output",
        ) as HTMLTextAreaElement;
        const status = document.getElementById("status")!;
        const formatBtn = document.getElementById("format-btn")!;
        const minifyBtn = document.getElementById("minify-btn")!;
        const copyBtn = document.getElementById("copy-btn")!;
        const clearBtn = document.getElementById("clear-btn")!;

        function showStatus(message: string, type: "success" | "error") {
            status.textContent = message;
            const color =
                type === "success" ? "text-green-600" : "text-red-600";
            status.className = "mt-4 text-sm font-medium " + color;
        }

        function clearStatus() {
            status.textContent = "";
            status.className = "mt-4 text-sm font-medium";
        }

        formatBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
            const text = input.value.trim();
            if (!text) {
                showStatus("Please enter some JSON.", "error");
                return;
            }
            try {
                const parsed = JSON.parse(text);
                output.value = JSON.stringify(parsed, null, 2);
                showStatus("✓ Valid JSON — formatted successfully.", "success");
            } catch (err) {
                output.value = "";
                showStatus(
                    "✗ Invalid JSON: " + (err as Error).message,
                    "error",
                );
            }
        });

        minifyBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
            const text = input.value.trim();
            if (!text) {
                showStatus("Please enter some JSON.", "error");
                return;
            }
            try {
                const parsed = JSON.parse(text);
                output.value = JSON.stringify(parsed);
                showStatus("✓ JSON minified successfully.", "success");
            } catch (err) {
                output.value = "";
                showStatus(
                    "✗ Invalid JSON: " + (err as Error).message,
                    "error",
                );
            }
        });

        copyBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
            if (output.value) {
                navigator.clipboard.writeText(output.value);
                showStatus("✓ Copied to clipboard.", "success");
            }
        });

        clearBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
            input.value = "";
            output.value = "";
            clearStatus();
            input.focus();
        });
    </script>

    <script
        type="application/ld+json"
        set:html={JSON.stringify({
            "@context": "https://schema.org",
            "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
            name: "JSON Formatter & Validator",
            applicationCategory: "DeveloperApplication",
            operatingSystem: "Any",
            description:
                "Free online JSON formatter and validator. Format, beautify, and validate JSON data instantly.",
            offers: {
                "@type": "Offer",
                price: "0",
                priceCurrency: "USD",
            },
        })}
    />

    <script
        type="application/ld+json"
        set:html={JSON.stringify({
            "@context": "https://schema.org",
            "@type": "FAQPage",
            mainEntity: [
                {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    name: "Is my JSON data safe?",
                    acceptedAnswer: {
                        "@type": "Answer",
                        text: "Yes. All formatting and validation happens in your browser. No data is sent to any server.",
                    },
                },
                {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    name: "What is JSON?",
                    acceptedAnswer: {
                        "@type": "Answer",
                        text: "JSON (JavaScript Object Notation) is a lightweight data format used to exchange data between servers and web applications.",
                    },
                },
                {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    name: "Does this tool support large JSON files?",
                    acceptedAnswer: {
                        "@type": "Answer",
                        text: "Yes, it can handle large JSON files. Performance depends on your browser and device memory.",
                    },
                },
            ],
        })}
    />
</Layout>
